{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544711-who-would-win","id":1544711,"title":"Who Would Win?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-25T02:02:14-07:00","id":1544711,"title":"Who Would Win?","content":"Alright, it was only a matter of time before someone brought this up. These conversations, and debates, have been happening for literal decades with WoD and then CoD. Now we have it with CB.<br /> <br /> Who are the best lineages and families in a fight? We have a lot of the mechanics at this point, so we can maybe have some idea about families and their relative fighting prowess.<br /> <br /> Traditionally, it\u2019s always been the shifters who had a massive advantage. In CB, it seems like there is more balance and parity.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s looking to me like the Hungry are pretty fierce in CB. A Vorare who gets a +1 physical advantage, has a flaming sword, regenerates 1 injury per round, and can heal himself when he damages enemies - that is pretty hard to beat.<br /> <br /> The Get of Lyka, of course, are going to be too contenders too.<br /> <br /> Aside from the \u201cwho would win?\u201d Discussion, are there any cool powers or builds that stand out as particularly useful in a fight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T03:39:27-07:00","id":1544715,"title":"","content":"The powers that immediately stand out to me, not for being flashy but for potentially breaking some core assumptions of combat are Life Bridge (Shared Wounds) which lets you inflict injuries on a target equal to the number of injuries you're currently suffering, breaking the 1-2 Damage Per Attack assumption in half, and Power Tap which lets you generate 1-3 CD in a single combat action when virtually all other methods take a full scene and are at least a little bit inconvenient. <br /> <br /> In terms of white room fights, very, very few builds have any way to deal with an incorporeal Dead spamming a 0-cost attack spell while invisible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T08:36:08-07:00","id":1544890,"title":"","content":"Another thought. If you can get Flit to zero cost (trivial for some Families) I think you might be just kind of immune to being attacked in almost any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T10:28:03-07:00","id":1544893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544711-who-would-win?p=1544890#post1544890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thought. If you can get Flit to zero cost (trivial for some Families) I think you might be just kind of immune to being attacked in almost any way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Unburdened can reduce bleed for Ethereal spells. They have access to Telelocation and Flit is Ethereal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T11:23:06-07:00","id":1544896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544711-who-would-win?p=1544893#post1544893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Unburdened can reduce bleed for Ethereal spells. They have access to Telelocation and Flit is Ethereal.</div> </div> </div> </div>How it works depends on what casting a spell &quot;reflexively as a reaction&quot; works. It seems you can definitely avoid all melee attacks, because you can cast it in response to &quot;aggressive actions&quot; which should include moving into melee range. It might or might not work on ranged attacks depending on whether the attack resolves before you cast it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T16:02:41-07:00","id":1544934,"title":"","content":"Here is what the book says on reflexive actions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Reflexive Actions </b> <br /> <br /> Some actions happen so quickly or are so trivial to do they don\u2019t take up a character\u2019s time. This could be anything from chatting while performing another task to pulling a pistol from a holster when the character enters a building. These are reflexive actions, and a character can take as many reflexive actions on her turn as she would like, at Storyguide discretion. </div> </div> </div>It sounds like it can be done as many times as the player wants without effort. So the character with Flit seems to be invulnerable to physical attacks. Of course it says Storyguide discretion and I\u2019m sure most would limit that mechanic in some way,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T16:55:08-07:00","id":1544943,"title":"","content":"It's not about how often you can do it, it's about timing. That is, do you have to take the hit first?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T17:44:42-07:00","id":1544947,"title":"","content":"Well, from the wording of the Flit power, it really suggests that you avoid the attack entirely. If you took the damage anyway, then Flit wouldn\u2019t be very good for characters who have to bleed CD to use it. Avoiding the attack for the cost of a curse die seems reasonable. Just teleporting after getting damaged isn\u2019t really worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 10-28-2024, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T04:21:19-07:00","id":1544960,"title":"","content":"Whether it's worth it or not isn't really the question, a fair few spells aren't worth it without a Motif discount. <br /> <br /> Like Smoke, for example, is also a fraction to being attacked that costs 1CD and all it does is impose a Minor Complication that causes your intent to either hit somebody else in your range band or fall prone, specifically *after* they've damaged you, and only if they don't buy off the complication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T07:54:09-07:00","id":1544976,"title":"","content":"Well, you have a good point, just because it isn't very good if it doesn't avoid damage doesn't mean that it isn't a correct rule interpretation. Bleeding a CD to teleport away but still take damage is underpowered, but not nearly as much as being immune to damage is unbalanced for those families that can do Flit for free.<br /> <br /> The flavor text of the power says &quot;The best defense is simply not being there; don\u2019t be in the path of the bullet, inside the burning building, in the way of the car.&quot; which suggests to me that it does allow damage to be avoided, but I admit it isn't absolutely clear.<br /> <br /> I do think that the Storyguide should probably do something if a character can never be attacked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T08:06:17-07:00","id":1544978,"title":"","content":"I think the most balanced reading that's closest to RAW might be that it works against melee attacks because you can react to them closing the distance but not against gunshots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T15:08:58-07:00","id":1545006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544711-who-would-win#post1544711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, it was only a matter of time before someone brought this up. These conversations, and debates, have been happening for literal decades with WoD and then CoD. Now we have it with CB.<br /> <br /> Who are the best lineages and families in a fight? We have a lot of the mechanics at this point, so we can maybe have some idea about families and their relative fighting prowess.<br /> <br /> Traditionally, it\u2019s always been the shifters who had a massive advantage. In CB, it seems like there is more balance and parity.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s looking to me like the Hungry are pretty fierce in CB. A Vorare who gets a +1 physical advantage, has a flaming sword, regenerates 1 injury per round, and can heal himself when he damages enemies - that is pretty hard to beat.<br /> <br /> The Get of Lyka, of course, are going to be too contenders too.<br /> <br /> Aside from the \u201cwho would win?\u201d Discussion, are there any cool powers or builds that stand out as particularly useful in a fight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Welp, time for my traditional questions: in what contexts? Fights don't take place in white room simulations.<br /> <br /> &quot;What about the Endless Jaunt?&quot;<br /> <br /> We don't talk about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T17:07:36-07:00","id":1545014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544711-who-would-win?p=1545006#post1545006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Welp, time for my traditional questions: in what contexts? Fights don't take place in white room simulations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was thinking more generally- - like discussing cool combat builds, combat spells, and combinations. Not necessarily white room fights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544711-who-would-win?p=1545006#post1545006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;What about the Endless Jaunt?&quot;<br /> <br /> We don't talk about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Long jaunt! Longer than you think! <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T05:56:55-08:00","id":1545246,"title":"","content":"Further to the &quot;fights don't take place in white room situations&quot; conversation, as ever it follows that the best combat build is the one that can *force* the White Room situation in their target.<br /> <br /> Soul Scry lets you observe any person or place you are even &quot;passingly familiar with&quot; for the cost of one CD, they cannot resist and nothing indicates they are even aware they are being observed.<br /> <br /> You may then cast spells with the Ethereal tag on the observed target, expending one additional CP per cast.<br /> <br /> Faceless and Furies both get CD reduction for Ethereal spells, making they can cast Ethereal spells at normal cost on anybody they are even &quot;passingly familiar with&quot;, with no retaliation.<br /> <br /> The Faceless can also take Power Tap to top up their CD as they go. They can't cast it through Soul Scry since it's not Ethereal but they can, like, keep a bucket of rats nearby.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Oh, or of course they could use Flexible Spellcasting to *give* Power Tap Etheral, letting to be used for free on the target through the Scrying window.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 11-03-2024, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-22T07:50:28-08:00","id":1546287,"title":"","content":"Not a power combo exactly but Executive Function is incredibly funny. <br /> <br /> As far as I can tell it means that you get to use your best dice pool for *everything you do*, as long as you're doing something that uses that dice pool at the same time.<br /> <br /> You do have to spend successes on both actions of you want them both to succeed but it should be fairly trivial to find a Difficulty 1 (or even Difficulty 0) action that you can combine with anything else you want to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-15T00:48:55-07:00","id":1558866,"title":"","content":"At this point and time, I'm gonna say that CB Sorcerers would beat Awakened Mages for one simple reason: <b>They don't suffer Paradox!</b><br /> <br /> Based on what reviews I've listened to, and research I've conducted, it seems like Sorcerers and Mages are on a relatively even playing field when it comes to their upward potential. The key difference between them however, is how often and how freely they are allowed to work their spells.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the Awakened, magic has to be used sparingly, while always taking the right precautions and safety measures.<br /> <br /> But in Curseborne, magic is something you are forced to rely on constantly, because you begin suffering from crippling withdrawal symptoms if you don't.<br /> <br /> <br /> One side will explode if they use too much magic, while the other side explodes if they use too little.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-15T08:35:34-07:00","id":1558869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544711-who-would-win?p=1558866#post1558866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point and time, I'm gonna say that CB Sorcerers would beat Awakened Mages for one simple reason: <b>They don't suffer Paradox!</b><br /> <br /> Based on what reviews I've listened to, and research I've conducted, it seems like Sorcerers and Mages are on a relatively even playing field when it comes to their upward potential. The key difference between them however, is how often and how freely they are allowed to work their spells.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the Awakened, magic has to be used sparingly, while always taking the right precautions and safety measures.<br /> <br /> But in Curseborne, magic is something you are forced to rely on constantly, because you begin suffering from crippling withdrawal symptoms if you don't.<br /> <br /> <br /> One side will explode if they use too much magic, while the other side explodes if they use too little.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That.....feels very different, having actually read the books.<br /> <br /> First of all, CB may not have Paradox exactly, but they do suffer complications for Fast Casting that effectively acts as Paradox-it's one of the biggest problems with triggering their Damnation and is quintessentially the reason they want to make their sacrfifices and wrap themselves in their curse.<br /> <br /> Second big thing, on the magic front, is that the Awakened* have some serious support structures for their magic. Sure, they have to contend with Paradox, but even there they have some pretty intense options for how to deal with it, and more importantly when it comes to their magic, they have a lot of ways to just get dice to make their spells do what they want, or just reinforce their magic in general.I could basically just wave a hand in the direction of Signs of Sorcery and point out that for all the non-core material that's in there, a lot of it just builds on core material as well, as an indicator of just how much stuff goes into and surrounds Awakened magic.<br /> <br /> As a sort of side note to that, while not every mage will avail themselves of the advantages of the Sectarian Orders/Ministries, even those who play around in Nameless Orders benefit from the fact that player characters aren't assumed to have an adverserial relationship with their major organizations of choice, and as such have a lot less issues when it comes to material supports-and taking advantage of the three major Sects and their Orders lends a whole fucking lot of material support. Sorcerers at the scale we've been presented with in Curseborne, by contrast, are assumed to be in some form of opposition and antagonism with their Families even if they are otherwise completely on board with the policies and directions of those organizations-Generational Conflict is a big deal in CB.<br /> <br /> But the bigger issue is that, and I say this with an understanding that we're missing what's effectively the Mastery Level of conversation in Curseborne, limited to Entanglement 4 while in Awakening* we can see all the way to 10, and including supplements also notates archmastery, but.....<br /> <br /> The Arcana are just a wider breadth of tools than the Invocation Practices of the Sorcerers and those Shares Spells they have with other Lineages, and the Awakened Practices of those Arcana is just way too versatile.<br /> <br /> Some of the Arcana don't even have proper representation in CB-Time and Fate are the big ones, but there are elements of all the Arcana that the Invocation Practices haven't touched yet, and Curseborne Practices are just a lot more rigid when it comes to what you can do with and in spells, built inherently more like the magics of other splats. Meanwhile, the Awakened's approach to spells being to take the subject matter and then play around with them in broad categorical approaches means that even within the limits of 1 Dot of an Arcana, Awakened can do a lot of things, and none of them insignificant.<br /> <br /> Now of course, it's worth noting that there's also a thematic divide here as well-the Awakened in Awakening and Ascension represent something of an elite extreme in comparison to their peers, Ascension Mages fighting a war to save the world(Bit of an exaggeration, yes), and Awakening Mages explicitly are a metaphysical 1% class. Sorcerers meanwhile are meant to be more on par with their peers in other Lineages, and ironically better fit the idea of magic casters in the Hellenistic Age. Sorcerers are not grand wizards steeped in Wisdom and the powers of gods long dead and defeated, philosopher kings in search of celestial thrones.They're hustlers and addicts with pragmatic concerns and works that need upkeep, hedge witches building their kingdoms<br /> <br /> So while, yes, the Awakened have to contend with Paradox, that's more a consequence of being able to <i>throttle the heavens</i>. The Sorcerers bow their head in mock modesty, and don't ask where the Awakened land when they trip-let them hang themselves on their own rope. They may only be able to reach the clouds, but their towers are <i>very nice.</i><br /> <br /> *I am also applying this to Ascension mages, because the twain are more similar than not, but Awakening is my backyard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-10-2026, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-15T10:40:44-07:00","id":1558871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544711-who-would-win?p=1558869#post1558869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ascension Mages fighting a war to save the world(Bit of an exaggeration, yes),</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really, considering the history of screw ups the Technocracy has been responsible for. Also the fact that the Progenitors are practically the only branch that hasn't been thoroughly corrupted from its original ideology by now.<br /> <br /> --------------------------<br /> <br /> Anyways, I thought I read something about how Sorcerers in CB have a similar flexibility with designing their spells to what Awakened have; but it sounds like that's not exactly the case?<br /> <br /> True, their towers may not be fashioned out of solid gold and studded gemstones, but at least they have the luxury of showing them off. Where as the Awakened are stuck lurking about in some parallel dimension because the paparazzi causes their sanctum to implode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-15T11:27:29-07:00","id":1558873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544711-who-would-win?p=1558871#post1558871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not really, considering the history of screw ups the Technocracy has been responsible for. Also the fact that the Progenitors are practically the only branch that hasn't been thoroughly corrupted from its original ideology by now.<br /> <br /> --------------------------<br /> <br /> Anyways, I thought I read something about how Sorcerers in CB have a similar flexibility with designing their spells to what Awakened have; but it sounds like that's not exactly the case?<br /> <br /> True, their towers may not be fashioned out of solid gold and studded gemstones, but at least they have the luxury of showing them off. Where as the Awakened are stuck lurking about in some parallel dimension because the paparazzi causes their sanctum to implode.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Sorcerers spells, and indeed the Accursed Spells overall, follow fixed forms of magic with linear progression expanding the base use of each spells. The Sorcerers do have an advantage in that they can mimic some spells briefly after experiencing it, but it's not freeform.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, while a more occult or more present supernatural environment is a matter of taste, Curseborne's general appeal towards being Masquerade-less has greatly done itself a favor in differentiating itself in the urban horror scene, and I think the Sorcerers being able to enjoy more of a public interaction is a great example of that. You couldn't have an organization like the Premiere in Awakening or Ascension, and attempts to do so would lead to a very different function of it, and while they're the ones to most benefit from that, layers of it still exist in most of the Families. Being able to be a part of the communities that benefit or suffer from your magic is a really sharp angle to the urban horror of the wizard flavor, and I do agree that being able to partake in that is something can be rewarding in all the ways throttling the heavens behind layers of mysteries can be. Sorcerers are my second favorite Lineage in Curseborne, after all.<br /> <br /> But then again, some people do want to throttle the heavens, and look good in mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-15T12:01:46-07:00","id":1558874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544711-who-would-win?p=1558873#post1558873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curseborne's general appeal towards being Masquerade-less has greatly done itself a favor in differentiating itself in the urban horror scene, and I think the Sorcerers being able to enjoy more of a public interaction is a great example of that.<br /> <br /> But then again, some people do want to throttle the heavens, and look good in mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, so there's no official code of secrecy for these things?<br /> <br /> I wonder how people react to that when it comes to Ghosts and Undead?<br /> <br /> Just the idea of it being public knowledge that somebody could die, then get back up and continue to go about their business.<br /> <br /> That's pretty amusing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T10:08:32-07:00","id":1558894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544711-who-would-win?p=1558874#post1558874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, so there's no official code of secrecy for these things?<br /> <br /> I wonder how people react to that when it comes to Ghosts and Undead?<br /> <br /> Just the idea of it being public knowledge that somebody could die, then get back up and continue to go about their business.<br /> <br /> That's pretty amusing!</div> </div> </div> </div>They treat it like a curse you don't want to catch.<br /> <br /> It's not quite an open secret, but there's no structural reinforcement of people not knowing about the supernatural, beyond the Families taking collective action if it becomes too much of an issue. The main reason the supernatural remains relatively secret is that people deal with curses on a semi-regular basis, knows it can hit hard, and it can seem arbitrary in how it can hit. People's impression of running into the supernatural is one of immediate and visceral <i>unfairness</i>, a case of stepping in it that exceeds the step. Going with the Ghosts and Undead example, people don't think of these dead as dying and getting back up to go about their business-seeing a ghost means <i>you're already in it</i> and things are about get very bad for you, running into a vampire might mean you might walk away with a plague that causes eyes to spill out of pustules in a few hours or your memories of your grandmother will be replaced with those of a demonic clown eating your organs in alphabetical order, smiling at you in a &quot;See you soon&quot; sort of way, even if you manage to get away from the vampire unscathed. Dealing with the supernatural too much can curse you with cancer, metaphorical or literal, it can change you for the irrevocable worse. The dead don't get up and go about their business as usual, the dead get up <i>and make things worse</i>.<br /> <br /> People deal with notices of the supernatural in the same way they deal with a burning building or rapidly flooding street-try to avoid it as much as possible. The rituals, practices, and superstitions of the world of Curseborne are survival tactics, tested and tried over millenia. If you suspect your co-worker might actually be a ghost riding someone else's course, the response is to politely pretend you don't actually think that, and decline to go out for drinks with them later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}